{
  "id": "typescript-17-strict-compiler-flags",
  "slug": "strict-compiler-flags",
  "title": "The strict flag family and what each option does",
  "moduleId": "typescript-17-compiler-options-tooling",
  "order": 1,
  "hook": "**`strict`: true** enables strictNullChecks, noImplicitAny, strictFunctionTypes, and more. Senior engineers explain each flag and how they differ from C# NRT (compile-time only).",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "What is this?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "**strict** bundle turns on ~7 options including strictNullChecks, noImplicitAny, strictPropertyInitialization, useUnknownInCatchVariables. Enable individually for migration. strictNullChecks makes null/undefined explicit. Unlike C# NRT — no runtime enforcement."
        },
        {
          "type": "glossary",
          "title": "Key terms",
          "entries": [
            {
              "term": "strictNullChecks",
              "longForm": "null safety",
              "plainDefinition": "null/undefined not assignable without union.",
              "example": "string ≠ string|null"
            },
            {
              "term": "noImplicitAny",
              "longForm": "ban implicit any",
              "plainDefinition": "Untyped params error.",
              "example": "function f(x) // error"
            },
            {
              "term": "strictFunctionTypes",
              "longForm": "callback safety",
              "plainDefinition": "Contravariant param checking.",
              "example": "handler assignability"
            },
            {
              "term": "strictPropertyInitialization",
              "longForm": "class fields",
              "plainDefinition": "Fields init in ctor or definite assignment.",
              "example": "name!: string"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Why does it matter?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "strict false accumulates any/null bugs. FAANG enforces strict. C# devs need validation at boundaries despite compile checks."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "tip",
          "title": "Interview trap: strict = runtime",
          "body": "strictNullChecks does not stop JSON null at runtime."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How it works step by step",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "title": "Mental model",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "strict true new projects",
              "body": "Enable strict and the full family on greenfield repos — migrate legacy code incrementally with eslint overrides."
            },
            {
              "title": "migrate per-flag",
              "body": "strictNullChecks first"
            },
            {
              "title": "fix with guards",
              "body": "unknown boundaries"
            },
            {
              "title": "CI tsc",
              "body": "enforce"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "type": "mermaid",
            "title": "strict family",
            "source": "flowchart TD\n  S[strict] --> N[noImplicitAny]\n  S --> NS[strictNullChecks]\n  S --> SF[strictFunctionTypes]\n  S --> U[useUnknownInCatchVariables]"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Code walkthrough",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "json",
            "label": "strict tsconfig",
            "code": "{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"noUncheckedIndexedAccess\": true\n  }\n}",
            "explanation": "strict + extra flags."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "strictNullChecks",
            "code": "function greet(n: string) { return n.toUpperCase(); }\nconst x: string | null = get();\nif (x !== null) greet(x);",
            "explanation": "Narrow null before use."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "noImplicitAny",
            "code": "function process(data: unknown) {\n  if (typeof data === \"string\") return data.length;\n  throw new Error();\n}",
            "explanation": "unknown not implicit any."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Failure: strict false",
            "code": "function parse(x) { return JSON.parse(x); } // any chain",
            "explanation": "implicit any poisons inference."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
